<Legal
    title="Delete your account"
    description="How to delete your Sikemux account, and what is deleted when you do."
    updated="3 October 2026">
    <p>
        To delete your Sikemux account, email <a href="mailto:contact@nodelike.com">contact@nodelike.com</a> from the address you sign in with and say you want the account deleted. We will reply to confirm it is you.
    </p>

    <h2>What we delete</h2>
    <p>Within 30 days of your request we delete:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            your account: your email address, the name and profile picture Google or GitHub shared, and your password
            hash if you chose a password;
        </li>
        <li>every device on the account, with its name, platform and key;</li>
        <li>the record of devices added to and removed from the account, and your sign-in sessions.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We email you when it is done.</p>
    <p>
        Server logs that mention your account are not deleted one by one. They are deleted automatically as newer logs
        replace them. Backups of the account database are kept for 30 days, so your account is gone from them within 30
        days too.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your devices</h2>
    <p>
        Deleting your account does not touch anything on your computer or phone. Your code, files, terminals and agent
        chats never reached us. Uninstall the apps to remove them.
    </p>

    <h2>Removing one phone</h2>
    <p>To take just one phone off your account, sign out of the Sikemux phone app on it.</p>

    <p>Deleting your account from inside the apps is on its way. Until then, email us as above.</p>
    <p>More about what we keep is in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</Legal>
